# kex: check-only
# A `let` of an uppercase name is a constant only when `=` (or a type) comes
# next. `let HELLO - 16`, a typo for `=`, was taken as a constant with no
# body, passed `--check`, and failed in lowering with a mangled C++ name
# (kexhq/kex#701). It is a syntax error at the `-`.

main do
  let HELLO - 16

  IO.printLine("Hello, ${22 / (HELLO - 16)}")
end
